# ~/.clauderc_file_structure — Claude-maintained repo registry
# Counterpart to ~/.clauderc (paths/constants) and ~/.clauderc_context (context, TBD).
# Sourced the same way. Mine to edit freely — no permission needed.
#
# Purpose: canonical (local_path, github_url) pairs, one per tracked repo.
# .clauderc's REPO SHORTCUTS section gives quick $VARS for cd/scripts;
# this file is the fuller record — local disk location + remote origin
# together, so a repo's identity doesn't require re-deriving `git remote -v`.

